From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Thu, 2 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: the opponent binding covers the Normal Summon and Set
 procedures (Ra Sphere Mode), and a summon bound to a seat that is gone does
 not happen at n > 2

The F5 binding only knew EFFECT_SPSUMMON_PROC. Ra Sphere Mode uses
EFFECT_LIMIT_SUMMON_PROC, so a Tribute from several opponents was offered and no
opponent was asked. The binding now covers EFFECT_SUMMON_PROC,
EFFECT_LIMIT_SUMMON_PROC, EFFECT_SET_PROC and EFFECT_LIMIT_SET_PROC too. SummonRule
and MonsterSet ask for the opponent and send the monster to that field.

When the bound seat is out of the duel (or has a pending loss) before the summon
completes, SummonRule, MonsterSet and SpSummonRule stop before the move: the card
stays in the hand and not in the Graveyard. 1v1 is unchanged.
---
 interpreter.cpp | 15 +++++++--
 operations.cpp  | 82 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/interpreter.cpp b/interpreter.cpp
index 6b9c533..013e7a9 100644
--- a/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/interpreter.cpp
@@ -445,11 +445,22 @@ static uint8_t scope_player_of(const field* gf, effect* peffect) {
 	const uint8_t P = peffect->get_handler_player();
 	return gf->is_duelist(P) ? P : DUELIST_NONE;
 }
-// F5: summon procedures with an opponent field (EFFECT_FLAG_SPSUM_PARAM and o_range), n > 2 only.
+// F5: summon, set and special summon procedures with an opponent field (EFFECT_FLAG_SPSUM_PARAM and o_range),
+// n > 2 only. The Normal Summon codes too (Ra Sphere Mode uses EFFECT_LIMIT_SUMMON_PROC).
 bool interpreter::is_proc_effect(effect* peffect) const {
 	const auto* gf = pduel->game_field;
-	if(!peffect || !gf || gf->n_duelists <= 2 || peffect->code != EFFECT_SPSUMMON_PROC)
+	if(!peffect || !gf || gf->n_duelists <= 2)
 		return false;
+	switch(peffect->code) {
+	case EFFECT_SPSUMMON_PROC:
+	case EFFECT_SUMMON_PROC:
+	case EFFECT_LIMIT_SUMMON_PROC:
+	case EFFECT_SET_PROC:
+	case EFFECT_LIMIT_SET_PROC:
+		break;
+	default:
+		return false;
+	}
 	return peffect->is_flag(EFFECT_FLAG_SPSUM_PARAM) && peffect->o_range;
 }
 uint8_t* interpreter::proc_slot(effect* peffect) {
diff --git a/operations.cpp b/operations.cpp
